// ─── ARTICLE CONTENT (long HTML) — translated for major languages ─────────────
const articleContent = {
  en: {
    a1: `<p>Technology has rapidly become the foundation of modern society, shaping the way people learn, work, and interact. For today's youth, digital learning is not just a privilege but a necessity. In communities across the globe, students are increasingly embracing digital tools that equip them with knowledge, confidence, and life-changing opportunities.</p><br><p>One of the greatest advantages of technology in education is accessibility. Online platforms, mobile applications, and interactive tools allow students in rural or underserved areas to connect with high-quality learning resources. This democratization of knowledge ensures that no young person is left behind, regardless of geography or socio-economic background.</p><br><p>Beyond accessibility, technology also fosters creativity and critical thinking. Through project-based learning, coding programs, and digital collaboration, youth can solve real-world problems and innovate with confidence. These skills extend beyond the classroom, empowering them to become leaders, entrepreneurs, and changemakers in their communities.</p><br><p>Moreover, technology is reshaping career paths. With industries demanding digital literacy, coding, data analysis, and AI knowledge, young people who embrace technology stand out in the workforce. By equipping youth with these future-ready skills, we prepare them for sustainable careers and enable them to contribute meaningfully to global development.</p><br><p>However, the journey is not without challenges. Many regions face issues such as limited internet connectivity, lack of devices, or inadequate training for educators. Overcoming these hurdles requires a collaborative effort between governments, NGOs, and private sectors to build infrastructure, provide training, and ensure equitable access.</p><br><p>Ultimately, transforming youth through technology learning is about more than just academic success. It's about building resilience, nurturing confidence, and creating opportunities for young people to thrive in an interconnected world. As we invest in digital education, we invest in a brighter, more inclusive future for all.</p>`,
    a2: `<p>Sustainability is no longer a buzzword; it is a call to action. Around the world, students are leading the charge in building eco-conscious communities and reshaping the way we think about the environment. From reducing plastic use to spearheading renewable energy campaigns, young people are proving that small steps can create meaningful global change.</p><br><p>One of the most powerful tools for sustainability lies in awareness. Students organizing campaigns, workshops, and green clubs are raising awareness about pressing issues such as climate change, waste reduction, and conservation. This peer-to-peer learning not only educates but also inspires entire communities to adopt eco-friendly practices.</p><br><p>Beyond awareness, action is critical. Many student-led initiatives focus on recycling programs, tree-planting drives, and energy conservation projects. In doing so, students learn valuable lessons about leadership and responsibility while directly impacting their local environment. These grassroots projects ripple outward, influencing families, neighborhoods, and policy discussions.</p><br><p>Technology also plays a significant role. Social media allows young activists to amplify their messages, connect with global networks, and advocate for systemic changes. Platforms like Instagram and TikTok have become spaces where sustainability movements gain momentum, empowering youth voices to reach policymakers and businesses alike.</p><br><p>Building sustainable communities requires collaboration. Students who work hand-in-hand with educators, local governments, and NGOs can scale their impact and create lasting change. Whether through eco-hackathons, clean energy prototypes, or awareness campaigns, their contributions highlight the creativity and determination of the next generation.</p><br><p>The ultimate impact of student-led sustainability is not only environmental but also social. By fostering responsibility, empathy, and a sense of collective purpose, students are cultivating communities that thrive on shared values. Their leadership proves that sustainability is not an option but an essential path toward a healthier and more equitable future.</p>`,
    a3: `<p>The future of global development is being shaped not only by policymakers and organizations but also by students. With innovation, determination, and digital fluency, today's youth are redefining the way societies address issues such as poverty, education, and equality. Their leadership is setting new trends that promise long-lasting impact worldwide.</p><br><p>One trend is the rise of social entrepreneurship. Students are launching startups that address local and global challenges, from clean water initiatives to sustainable farming solutions. These ventures not only solve pressing issues but also generate employment and foster innovation at the grassroots level.</p><br><p>Another trend is digital advocacy. Students are using online platforms to voice concerns about climate change, human rights, and gender equality. Their ability to mobilize audiences quickly has turned grassroots movements into global campaigns, influencing decision-makers and shaping public opinion.</p><br><p>Collaborative learning is also gaining traction. International student exchange programs, hackathons, and global forums are giving young people platforms to share ideas, challenge perspectives, and co-create solutions. These experiences broaden their worldview and prepare them to be inclusive leaders in diverse communities.</p><br><p>Technology plays a central role in amplifying these trends. With access to AI, data analysis, and virtual learning, students are building tools that predict problems and propose innovative solutions. Their ability to merge technology with social impact is redefining what development looks like in the 21st century.</p><br><p>As these trends gain momentum, it becomes clear that the role of students in global development is not marginal—it is essential. By empowering them with resources, mentorship, and opportunities, society can unlock the full potential of youth leadership. The future of development is bright, and it is undeniably student-led.</p>`,
    a4: `<p>Graduating is more than earning a degree; it's the beginning of a journey that often inspires change within communities. Around the world, graduates are using their skills, resilience, and stories of perseverance to spark meaningful transformation, proving that education is one of the most powerful tools for change.</p><br><p>Many graduates return to their hometowns with a vision to uplift their communities. Some open schools to provide better education for local children, while others launch social enterprises that address pressing issues like unemployment or healthcare. Their actions showcase how education extends beyond personal growth to collective advancement.</p><br><p>Stories of resilience also inspire others. Graduates who overcame poverty, discrimination, or other challenges often share their journeys, encouraging younger students to dream big and pursue education. These narratives not only motivate but also build a culture of persistence and hope.</p><br><p>Moreover, graduates play a crucial role in mentoring. By guiding younger students through internships, workshops, and volunteer programs, they ensure that the next generation has the tools and confidence to succeed. This cycle of mentorship strengthens community bonds and creates a ripple effect of progress.</p><br><p>In many cases, graduate journeys also contribute to global networks. By joining international organizations or research collaborations, they bring back knowledge and connections that further enrich local communities. Their ability to bridge the local and global fosters innovation and inclusion.</p><br><p>Ultimately, graduate stories highlight that success is not measured solely by personal achievement but by the positive change one brings to society. Their journeys inspire us to believe in the transformative power of education and to continue supporting learners at every stage of their path.</p>`,
    a5: `<p>Education is undergoing a paradigm shift, driven by technology and progressive teaching models. The traditional classroom layout is transforming into an interactive, digital space where learning is personalized, inclusive, and tailored for the future.</p><br><p>At the center of classroom innovation is gamification. Integrating educational games, quizzes, and simulations makes complex concepts engaging and memorable. Students are no longer passive listeners; they become active participants who explore ideas, solve challenges, and collaborate dynamically.</p><br><p>Another breakthrough is personalized learning. AI-driven platforms can analyze student performance and adjust learning paths accordingly. This ensures that fast learners remain challenged while students who need more support receive targeted guidance, creating a balanced and supportive classroom environment.</p><br><p>Virtual and augmented reality (VR/AR) are also expanding horizons. Students can now embark on virtual field trips to historic sites, dive deep into human anatomy, or explore molecular chemistry, turning abstract concepts into tangible experiences. This immersive approach deepens understanding and sparks curiosity.</p><br><p>Additionally, classroom innovation values digital literacy and ethics. Teaching students how to evaluate online sources, protect privacy, and engage respectfully online is as vital as academic content. This builds digital citizens prepared for the opportunities and responsibilities of the modern world.</p><br><p>Fostering this shift requires empowering educators. Providing training, modern equipment, and support allows teachers to lead innovative classrooms with confidence. When schools and communities invest in progressive education, they open pathways for students to achieve their potential and solve future global challenges.</p>`
  },
  es: {
    a1: `<p>La tecnología se ha convertido rápidamente en la base de la sociedad moderna, transformando la forma en que las personas aprenden, trabajan e interactúan. Para los jóvenes de hoy, el aprendizaje digital no es solo un privilegio, sino una necesidad. En comunidades de todo el mundo, los estudiantes adoptan cada vez más las herramientas digitales que los equipan con conocimiento, confianza y oportunidades que cambian su vida.</p><br><p>Una de las mayores ventajas de la tecnología en la educación es la accesibilidad. Las plataformas en línea, las aplicaciones móviles y las herramientas interactivas permiten a los estudiantes de zonas rurales o desatendidas acceder a recursos de aprendizaje de alta calidad. Esta democratización del conocimiento garantiza que ningún joven se quede atrás, independientemente de su ubicación geográfica o contexto socioeconómico.</p><br><p>Más allá de la accesibilidad, la tecnología también fomenta la creatividad y el pensamiento crítico. Mediante el aprendizaje basado en proyectos, los programas de programación y la colaboración digital, los jóvenes pueden resolver problemas del mundo real e innovar con confianza. Estas habilidades van más allá del aula, permitiéndoles convertirse en líderes, emprendedores y agentes de cambio en sus comunidades.</p><br><p>En última instancia, transformar a los jóvenes a través del aprendizaje tecnológico va más allá del éxito académico. Se trata de construir resiliencia, cultivar la confianza y crear oportunidades para que los jóvenes prosperen en un mundo interconectado.</p>`,
    a2: `<p>La sostenibilidad ya no es una palabra de moda; es un llamado a la acción. En todo el mundo, los estudiantes lideran la construcción de comunidades ecológicamente conscientes y transforman nuestra forma de pensar sobre el medio ambiente. Desde reducir el uso de plástico hasta encabezar campañas de energía renovable, los jóvenes demuestran que los pequeños pasos pueden crear cambios globales significativos.</p><br><p>Una de las herramientas más poderosas para la sostenibilidad es la concienciación. Los estudiantes que organizan campañas, talleres y clubes ecológicos sensibilizan sobre problemas urgentes como el cambio climático, la reducción de residuos y la conservación. Este aprendizaje entre pares no solo educa, sino que también inspira a comunidades enteras a adoptar prácticas respetuosas con el medio ambiente.</p><br><p>El impacto final de la sostenibilidad liderada por estudiantes no solo es ambiental, sino también social. Al fomentar la responsabilidad, la empatía y un sentido de propósito colectivo, los estudiantes cultivan comunidades que prosperan en valores compartidos.</p>`,
    a3: `<p>El futuro del desarrollo global está siendo moldeado no solo por los responsables políticos y las organizaciones, sino también por los estudiantes. Con innovación, determinación y fluidez digital, los jóvenes de hoy redefinen la forma en que las sociedades abordan problemas como la pobreza, la educación y la igualdad.</p><br><p>Una tendencia es el auge del emprendimiento social. Los estudiantes están creando startups que abordan desafíos locales y globales, desde iniciativas de agua potable hasta soluciones de agricultura sostenible. Estas empresas no solo resuelven problemas urgentes, sino que también generan empleo y fomentan la innovación a nivel local.</p><br><p>A medida que estas tendencias ganan impulso, queda claro que el papel de los estudiantes en el desarrollo global no es marginal, sino esencial. El futuro del desarrollo es brillante y, sin duda, está liderado por los estudiantes.</p>`,
    a4: `<p>Graduarse es más que obtener un título; es el comienzo de un viaje que a menudo inspira cambios en las comunidades. En todo el mundo, los graduados utilizan sus habilidades, resiliencia e historias de perseverancia para generar transformaciones significativas, demostrando que la educación es una de las herramientas más poderosas para el cambio.</p><br><p>Muchos graduados regresan a sus ciudades natales con una visión para elevar a sus comunidades. Algunos abren escuelas para brindar mejor educación a los niños locales, mientras que otros lanzan empresas sociales que abordan problemas urgentes como el desempleo o la atención médica.</p><br><p>En última instancia, las historias de los graduados destacan que el éxito no se mide solo por los logros personales, sino por el cambio positivo que uno aporta a la sociedad.</p>`,
    a5: `<p>La educación está experimentando un cambio de paradigma, impulsado por la tecnología y los modelos pedagógicos progresistas. El diseño tradicional del aula se está transformando en un espacio digital e interactivo donde el aprendizaje es personalizado, inclusivo y adaptado al futuro.</p><br><p>En el centro de la innovación en el aula está la gamificación. La integración de juegos educativos, cuestionarios y simulaciones hace que los conceptos complejos sean atractivos y memorables. Los estudiantes ya no son oyentes pasivos; se convierten en participantes activos que exploran ideas, resuelven desafíos y colaboran dinámicamente.</p><br><p>Fomentar este cambio requiere empoderar a los educadores. Proporcionar capacitación, equipos modernos y apoyo permite a los docentes liderar aulas innovadoras con confianza.</p>`
  },
  fr: {
    a1: `<p>La technologie est rapidement devenue le fondement de la société moderne, façonnant la manière dont les gens apprennent, travaillent et interagissent. Pour les jeunes d'aujourd'hui, l'apprentissage numérique n'est pas seulement un privilège, mais une nécessité. Dans les communautés du monde entier, les étudiants adoptent de plus en plus les outils numériques qui les dotent de connaissances, de confiance et d'opportunités qui changent leur vie.</p><br><p>L'un des plus grands avantages de la technologie dans l'éducation est l'accessibilité. Les plateformes en ligne, les applications mobiles et les outils interactifs permettent aux étudiants des zones rurales ou mal desservies d'accéder à des ressources d'apprentissage de haute qualité. Cette démocratisation du savoir garantit qu'aucun jeune n'est laissé pour compte, quelle que soit sa situation géographique ou socio-économique.</p><br><p>En fin de compte, transformer les jeunes grâce à l'apprentissage technologique est bien plus que la réussite académique. Il s'agit de développer la résilience, de cultiver la confiance et de créer des opportunités pour les jeunes de s'épanouir dans un monde interconnecté.</p>`,
    a2: `<p>La durabilité n'est plus un simple mot à la mode ; c'est un appel à l'action. Partout dans le monde, les étudiants sont à l'avant-garde de la construction de communautés écologiquement conscientes. Des campagnes de réduction du plastique aux initiatives d'énergie renouvelable, les jeunes prouvent que de petites actions peuvent créer des changements mondiaux significatifs.</p><br><p>L'un des outils les plus puissants pour la durabilité est la sensibilisation. Les étudiants qui organisent des campagnes, des ateliers et des clubs verts sensibilisent aux problèmes urgents tels que le changement climatique et la conservation. L'impact final de la durabilité menée par les étudiants n'est pas seulement environnemental mais aussi social.</p>`,
    a3: `<p>L'avenir du développement mondial est façonné non seulement par les décideurs politiques et les organisations, mais aussi par les étudiants. Avec innovation, détermination et maîtrise du numérique, les jeunes d'aujourd'hui redéfinissent la manière dont les sociétés abordent des problèmes tels que la pauvreté, l'éducation et l'égalité.</p><br><p>Une tendance est l'essor de l'entrepreneuriat social. Les étudiants lancent des startups qui répondent à des défis locaux et mondiaux. Il est clair que le rôle des étudiants dans le développement mondial n'est pas marginal — il est essentiel. L'avenir du développement est brillant et indéniablement mené par les étudiants.</p>`,
    a4: `<p>Obtenir son diplôme est bien plus qu'acquérir un titre ; c'est le début d'un parcours qui inspire souvent le changement dans les communautés. Partout dans le monde, les diplômés utilisent leurs compétences, leur résilience et leurs histoires de persévérance pour susciter des transformations significatives.</p><br><p>De nombreux diplômés retournent dans leurs villes natales avec une vision pour élever leurs communautés. En fin de compte, les histoires de diplômés soulignent que le succès ne se mesure pas uniquement aux réalisations personnelles, mais au changement positif que l'on apporte à la société.</p>`,
    a5: `<p>L'éducation connaît un changement de paradigme, porté par la technologie et des modèles pédagogiques progressifs. La disposition traditionnelle de la salle de classe se transforme en un espace numérique interactif où l'apprentissage est personnalisé, inclusif et adapté à l'avenir.</p><br><p>Au cœur de l'innovation en classe se trouve la gamification. L'intégration de jeux éducatifs, de quiz et de simulations rend les concepts complexes engageants et mémorables. Les étudiants ne sont plus des auditeurs passifs ; ils deviennent des participants actifs. Favoriser ce changement nécessite d'autonomiser les éducateurs en leur fournissant formation, équipements modernes et soutien.</p>`
  },
  de: {
    a1: `<p>Technologie ist schnell zur Grundlage der modernen Gesellschaft geworden und prägt die Art und Weise, wie Menschen lernen, arbeiten und interagieren. Für die Jugend von heute ist digitales Lernen nicht nur ein Privileg, sondern eine Notwendigkeit. In Gemeinschaften auf der ganzen Welt nutzen Studierende zunehmend digitale Werkzeuge, die sie mit Wissen, Selbstvertrauen und lebensverändernden Möglichkeiten ausstatten.</p><br><p>Einer der größten Vorteile der Technologie im Bildungsbereich ist die Zugänglichkeit. Online-Plattformen, mobile Anwendungen und interaktive Tools ermöglichen es Studierenden in ländlichen oder unterversorgten Gebieten, auf hochwertige Lernressourcen zuzugreifen. Letztlich geht es darum, Resilienz aufzubauen, Selbstvertrauen zu fördern und Chancen für junge Menschen zu schaffen, in einer vernetzten Welt zu gedeihen.</p>`,
    a2: `<p>Nachhaltigkeit ist kein bloßes Schlagwort mehr; es ist ein Aufruf zum Handeln. Weltweit führen Studierende den Aufbau umweltbewusster Gemeinschaften an. Von der Reduzierung des Plastikverbrauchs bis hin zu Kampagnen für erneuerbare Energien beweisen junge Menschen, dass kleine Schritte bedeutende globale Veränderungen bewirken können.</p><br><p>Die letztendliche Wirkung der von Studierenden geführten Nachhaltigkeit ist nicht nur ökologisch, sondern auch sozial. Durch die Förderung von Verantwortung, Empathie und einem Sinn für kollektiven Zweck kultivieren Studierende Gemeinschaften, die auf gemeinsamen Werten gedeihen.</p>`,
    a3: `<p>Die Zukunft der globalen Entwicklung wird nicht nur von Politikern und Organisationen, sondern auch von Studierenden geprägt. Mit Innovation, Entschlossenheit und digitaler Kompetenz definieren die Jugendlichen von heute neu, wie Gesellschaften mit Problemen wie Armut, Bildung und Gleichheit umgehen.</p><br><p>Es wird deutlich, dass die Rolle der Studierenden in der globalen Entwicklung nicht marginal ist – sie ist wesentlich. Die Zukunft der Entwicklung ist rosig und unbestreitbar studierendengeführt.</p>`,
    a4: `<p>Einen Abschluss zu machen ist mehr als nur einen Titel zu erwerben; es ist der Beginn einer Reise, die oft Veränderungen in Gemeinschaften inspiriert. Weltweit nutzen Absolventinnen und Absolventen ihre Fähigkeiten, Resilienz und Durchhaltegeschichten, um bedeutende Transformationen anzustoßen.</p><br><p>Letztendlich zeigen die Geschichten der Absolventinnen und Absolventen, dass Erfolg nicht nur an persönlichen Leistungen gemessen wird, sondern an dem positiven Wandel, den man in die Gesellschaft einbringt.</p>`,
    a5: `<p>Bildung durchläuft einen Paradigmenwechsel, der von Technologie und progressiven Lehrmodellen vorangetrieben wird. Das traditionelle Klassenzimmer wandelt sich in einen interaktiven, digitalen Raum, in dem Lernen personalisiert, inklusiv und zukunftsorientiert ist.</p><br><p>Im Mittelpunkt der Unterrichtsinnovation steht die Gamification. Die Integration von Lernspielen, Quiz und Simulationen macht komplexe Konzepte ansprechend und einprägsam. Diesen Wandel zu fördern erfordert die Stärkung der Lehrenden durch Training, moderne Ausstattung und Unterstützung.</p>`
  },
  pt: {
    a1: `<p>A tecnologia tornou-se rapidamente a base da sociedade moderna, moldando a forma como as pessoas aprendem, trabalham e interagem. Para os jovens de hoje, o aprendizado digital não é apenas um privilégio, mas uma necessidade. Em comunidades ao redor do mundo, os estudantes estão adotando ferramentas digitais que os equipam com conhecimento, confiança e oportunidades transformadoras.</p><br><p>Uma das maiores vantagens da tecnologia na educação é a acessibilidade. Plataformas online, aplicativos móveis e ferramentas interativas permitem que estudantes em áreas rurais ou carentes acessem recursos de aprendizagem de alta qualidade. Em última análise, transformar jovens por meio do aprendizado tecnológico é sobre construir resiliência e criar oportunidades em um mundo interconectado.</p>`,
    a2: `<p>A sustentabilidade não é mais apenas uma palavra da moda; é um chamado à ação. Em todo o mundo, estudantes estão liderando a construção de comunidades ecologicamente conscientes. De campanhas de redução do plástico a iniciativas de energia renovável, os jovens provam que pequenos passos podem criar mudanças globais significativas.</p><br><p>O impacto final da sustentabilidade liderada por estudantes não é apenas ambiental, mas também social. Ao promover responsabilidade, empatia e senso de propósito coletivo, os estudantes cultivam comunidades que prosperam em valores compartilhados.</p>`,
    a3: `<p>O futuro do desenvolvimento global está sendo moldado não apenas por formuladores de políticas, mas também por estudantes. Com inovação, determinação e fluência digital, os jovens de hoje redefinem como as sociedades abordam problemas como pobreza, educação e igualdade.</p><br><p>Fica claro que o papel dos estudantes no desenvolvimento global não é marginal — é essencial. O futuro do desenvolvimento é brilhante e inegavelmente liderado pelos estudantes.</p>`,
    a4: `<p>Graduar-se é mais do que conquistar um diploma; é o início de uma jornada que frequentemente inspira mudanças nas comunidades. Em todo o mundo, graduados usam suas habilidades, resiliência e histórias de perseverança para impulsionar transformações significativas.</p><br><p>Em última análise, as histórias dos graduados destacam que o sucesso não é medido apenas pelas realizações pessoais, mas pela mudança positiva que se traz à sociedade.</p>`,
    a5: `<p>A educação está passando por uma mudança de paradigma, impulsionada pela tecnologia e por modelos de ensino progressistas. O layout tradicional da sala de aula está se transformando em um espaço digital interativo onde o aprendizado é personalizado, inclusivo e adequado ao futuro.</p><br><p>No centro da inovação em sala de aula está a gamificação. A integração de jogos educacionais, quizzes e simulações torna conceitos complexos envolventes e memoráveis. Fomentar essa mudança requer empoderar os educadores com treinamento, equipamentos modernos e suporte.</p>`
  }
};

